  "title": "Orthogonality screen \u2014 locating the (1,1,0) leak",
  "updatedAt": "2026-07-14T12:00:00.000Z",
  "storage": {
    "type": "database",
    "table": "pages",
    "id": "corpus-13-orthogonality-screen"
  },
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Orthogonality screen \u2014 locating the (1,1,0) leak"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Directive \u2014 Attribute the leak to a specific interaction rather than to the gate as a whole."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Approach"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pairwise: each regulator against each non-cognate promoter, one interaction per well. Nine combinations, four replicates."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Single-interaction resolution is the point. A whole-gate measurement can only say the gate leaks; it can never say which part to change."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Result"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "mention",
            "attrs": {
              "id": "sample-4d0b00cd",
              "label": "C0062 (LuxR)",
              "entityType": "sequence",
              "entityId": "sample-4d0b00cd",
              "path": "sequences/kits/moclo-cidar/C0062_CD"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " activates "
          },
          {
            "type": "mention",
            "attrs": {
              "id": "sample-84f9f52b",
              "label": "R0040 (pTet)",
              "entityType": "sequence",
              "entityId": "sample-84f9f52b",
              "path": "sequences/kits/moclo-cidar/R0040_AB"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at 6 percent of its cognate activity. Nothing else exceeds 1 percent."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "That single interaction accounts for the entire (1,1,0) excess measured in entry 12 \u2014 an independent confirmation, not a fitted explanation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Options"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Swap "
          },
          {
            "type": "mention",
            "attrs": {
              "id": "sample-4d0b00cd",
              "label": "C0062 (LuxR)",
              "entityType": "sequence",
              "entityId": "sample-4d0b00cd",
              "path": "sequences/kits/moclo-cidar/C0062_CD"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for an orthogonal activator, at the cost of re-characterising an input; or accept a 26-fold gate with one asymmetric state. Entry 15 needs the LuxR input specifically, so the swap is deferred and the asymmetry documented."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Related entries"
